0008: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0009:     """Complete the dominant-color object by adding its left-right mirror image.
0010: 
0011:     Input structure
0012:     A rectangular grid contains one uniquely most frequent color forming the main
0013:     foreground object, with other colors acting as clutter/noise.
0014: 
0015:     Rule
0016:     Reflect every pixel of the dominant color across the vertical centerline of
0017:     the grid and recolor the reflected cells with that same dominant color.
0018: 
0019:     Key insight
0020:     The noisy cells are exactly the missing counterpart pixels needed to make the
0021:     dominant-color mask horizontally symmetric.
